## Ingredients

- 2 Cups Rolled Oats (aka Old Fashioned Oats)
- 1/2 cup Whole Wheat Flour / Oat flour
- 2 Tbs chia seeds / Flaxseeds -- this is the binder for the bars
- 2 tsp Ground Cinnamon
- 1/2 tsp Baking Powder
- 1/4 tsp Salt
- 1/3 cup Granulated sugar-free sweetener
  - monk fruit blend
- 2 Large Eggs (beaten)
- 1/3 cup melted Unsalted butter
- 1 tsp Pure Vanilla Extract

### Optional Mix-ins (1/2 Cup total max)

I like a mix of dark chocolate chips and walnuts personally

- chopped walnuts
- chopped pecans
- dark chocolate chips
- unseetened glaked coconut

## Instructions

Preheat oven to 350°F 

1. line 8x8 inch baking pan with parchment paper leaving a little overhand on the sides so that its easy to lift the bars out later.
2. Combine Dry Ingredients: in a large bowl mix:
   - rolled oats
   - flour
   - chia/flax seeds
   - cinnamon
   - baking powder
   - salt
   - sweetner
   - mix-ins
3. Combine Wet Ingredients: in a smaller bowl mix:
   - whisk the beaten eggs
   - melted butter (make sure its not boiling)
   - vanilla extract
4. Mix all togeather: pour the wet ingredients into the dry and stir thoroughly.
5. let stand for about 5 mins to ensure all the wet is well absorbed into the dry.
6. Press into Pan: transfer the mixture into the lined baking pan and use the back of a sturdy spatula to press the mixture down as girmly as possible.
7. bake for 22 - 25 mins or until the edges are golden brown and the center feels girm to the touch.
8. Coool and slice: allow the bars to cool complletely in the pan. Once cool, use the parchment paper handles to lift the block out onto a cutting board. Use a sharp chef's knife to slice into 12 bars

## Storage

- Shelf life: they will keep well in an airtight container at room tempature for 4 days or in the refrigerator for up to a month. Freeze for longer periods of time.
- I will wrap indivual bars tightly in parchment paper or reusable silicone bags for traveling.
